        "problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=\\frac{3}{1-5x}+\\frac{3}{4}?$",
        "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{3}{4},$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{3}{4})\\cup (\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929417/assets/00f66fd1de73592b3e0113b56ee23f334c2643b1e55fc185dfa9b9126d6ad680.png)",
